IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa9-circulation.l4: Companies Act 2006 (UK), Part 15 Chapter 7, first half: the duty to circulate copies of
-- accounts and reports, and the option to provide the strategic report with supplementary material
-- (ss 423, 424, 425, 426, 426A), lines 5658-5706 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa9-strategic.l4. Section 424(1) is a lead-in sentence (inert, reason 1), s 426(3) and (6) are
-- regulation-making provisions (inert, reason 2) and s 426(4) is blank in this text.
--
-- REGULATIVE RULES. Section 424(3) (a public company's 21 days) is also written as a regulative rule, `s 424(3) the public company
-- must send out copies`, run with #TRACE in coa9-tests-circulation.l4. A #TRACE prints FULFILLED or BREACH and adds no assertion
-- line to the counts check.sh prints, so the same duty is a decision function (`s 424(3) the public company sent the copies out in time`)
-- whose answers are asserted. The clock of the rule counts days from the day the obligation arises.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 423: Duty to circulate copies of annual accounts and reports
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 423 Duty to circulate copies of annual accounts and reports`

-- src:5660 | 423 Duty to circulate copies of annual accounts and reports
-- src:5661 | (1) Every company must send a copy of its annual accounts and reports for each financial year to—
-- src:5662 | (a) every member of the company,
-- src:5663 | (b) every holder of the company's debentures, and
-- src:5664 | (c) every person who is entitled to receive notice of general meetings.
@ref s 423(1) Every company must send a copy of its annual accounts and reports to its members, debenture holders and those entitled to notice of general meetings (src:5660-5664)
GIVEN `s 112 the person is a member of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a holder of the company's debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423(1) the company must send the person a copy of its annual accounts and reports for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `s 112 the person is a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the person is a holder of the company's debentures`
       OR `the person is entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 112 the person is a member of the company` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a member is decided by section 112
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty runs to "every member", "every holder of the company's debentures" and "every person who is entitled to receive notice of general meetings" and the list is not closed with "only"

-- src:5665 | (2) Copies need not be sent to a person for whom the company does not have a current address.
@ref s 423(2) Copies need not be sent to a person for whom the company has no current address (src:5665)
GIVEN `s 423(3) the company has a current address for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423(2) copies need not be sent to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 423(3) the company has a current address for the person`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Copies need not be sent to a person for whom the company does not have a current address"; the subsection says nothing of a person for whom it does
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the question of a current address was not answered

-- src:5666 | (3) A company has a “current address” for a person if—
-- src:5667 | (a) an address has been notified to the company by the person as one at which documents may be sent to him, and
-- src:5668 | (b) the company has no reason to believe that documents sent to him at that address will not reach him.
@ref s 423(3) Meaning of "current address" (src:5666-5668)
GIVEN `an address has been notified to the company by the person as one at which documents may be sent to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has no reason to believe that documents sent to him at that address will not reach him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423(3) the company has a current address for the person` MEANS
    IF `an address has been notified to the company by the person as one at which documents may be sent to him`
       AND `the company has no reason to believe that documents sent to him at that address will not reach him`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "A company has a “current address” for a person if— (a) an address has been notified ..., and (b) the company has no reason to believe that documents sent to him at that address will not reach him"

-- src:5669 | (4) In the case of a company not having a share capital, copies need not be sent to anyone who is not entitled to receive notices of general meetings of the company.
@ref s 423(4) A company without a share capital need not send copies to a person not entitled to notices of general meetings (src:5669)
GIVEN `the company does not have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to receive notices of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423(4) copies need not be sent to the person` MEANS
    IF `the company does not have a share capital` AND NOT (`the person is entitled to receive notices of general meetings of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company not having a share capital, copies need not be sent to anyone who is not entitled to receive notices of general meetings of the company"

-- src:5670 | (5) Where copies are sent out over a period of days, references in the Companies Acts to the day on which copies are sent out shall be read as references to the last day of that period.
@ref s 423(5) Copies sent out over a period of days: the day on which copies are sent out is the last day of the period (src:5670)
GIVEN `copies are sent out over a period of days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 423(5) the day on which copies are sent out` MEANS
    IF `copies are sent out over a period of days`
    THEN JUST `the last day of that period`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where copies are sent out over a period of days"; copies sent out on a single day are not mentioned

-- src:5671 | (6) This section has effect subject to section 426 (option to provide strategic report with supplementary material).
@ref s 423(6) Section 423 has effect subject to section 426 (src:5671)
GIVEN `the company provides a copy of the strategic report with supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports under section 426` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423(6) section 423 gives way to section 426 in the case` MEANS
    IF `the company provides a copy of the strategic report with supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports under section 426`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect subject to section 426"; where section 426 is not used the subsection says nothing

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 424: Time allowed for sending out copies of accounts and reports
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 424 Time allowed for sending out copies of accounts and reports`

-- (1) "The time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports is as follows." is a lead-in (inert, reason 1).

@ref s 423(6) Section 423 has effect subject to section 426 (src:5671)
DECLARE `s 424(5) time allowed` IS ONE OF
    `s 424(5) the time allowed for a private company`
    `s 424(5) the time allowed for a public company`

-- src:5679 | (5) Whether the time allowed is that for a private company or a public company is determined by reference to the company's status immediately before the end of the accounting reference period by reference to which the financial year for the accounts in question was determined.
@ref s 424(5) Whether the time allowed is that for a private or a public company (src:5679)
-- SEAM (PLAN 4.1): section 4(2). The caller answers it for the moment the text names: immediately before the end of the accounting reference period
-- by reference to which the financial year for the accounts in question was determined.
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 424(5) time allowed`
`s 424(5) whether the time allowed is that for a private company or a public company` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN `s 424(5) the time allowed for a public company`
    ELSE `s 424(5) the time allowed for a private company` -- a private company is any company that is not a public company (s 4(1))

-- src:5674 | (2) A private company must comply with section 423 not later than—
-- src:5675 | (a) the end of the period for filing accounts and reports, or
-- src:5676 | (b) if earlier, the date on which it actually delivers its accounts and reports to the registrar.
@ref s 424(2) A private company must comply with section 423 not later than the end of the period for filing or, if earlier, the date it delivers its accounts to the registrar (src:5674-5676)
GIVEN `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company actually delivers its accounts and reports to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 424(2) the last day on which a private company may send out copies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the company actually delivers its accounts and reports to the registrar`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports`
    WHEN JUST delivered THEN
        IF delivered AT MOST `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports`
        THEN delivered
        ELSE `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports`

@ref s 424(2) (src:5674)
GIVEN `the day on which copies were sent out` IS A DATE
      `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company actually delivers its accounts and reports to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 424(2) the private company sent the copies out in time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which copies were sent out` AT MOST `s 424(2) the last day on which a private company may send out copies` `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` `the date on which the company actually delivers its accounts and reports to the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "A private company must comply with section 423 not later than— (a) the end of the period for filing accounts and reports, or (b) if earlier, the date on which it actually delivers its accounts and reports to the registrar"

-- src:5677 | (3) A public company must comply with section 423 at least 21 days before the date of the relevant accounts meeting.
@ref s 424(3) A public company must comply with section 423 at least 21 days before the relevant accounts meeting (src:5677)
GIVEN `the date of the relevant accounts meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 424(3) the last day on which a public company may send out copies` MEANS
    `the date of the relevant accounts meeting` MINUS 21 -- fork F20: "at least 21 days before the date" is read as the meeting date less 21 days, not 21 clear days

@ref s 424(3) (src:5677)
GIVEN `the day on which copies were sent out` IS A DATE
      `the date of the relevant accounts meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 424(3) the public company sent the copies out in time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which copies were sent out` AT MOST `s 424(3) the last day on which a public company may send out copies` `the date of the relevant accounts meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "A public company must comply with section 423 at least 21 days before the date of the relevant accounts meeting"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The clock counts days from `the day the obligation arises`; the deadline is the last day on which
-- a public company may send copies out (21 days before the meeting).
@ref s 424(3) A public company must comply with section 423 at least 21 days before the relevant accounts meeting (src:5677)
DECLARE `s 424(3) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 424(3) send out copies of the annual accounts and reports`

@ref s 424(3) (src:5677)
GIVEN `the day the obligation arises` IS A DATE
      `the date of the relevant accounts meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 424(3) action`
`s 424(3) the public company must send out copies` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 424(3) send out copies of the annual accounts and reports`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 424(3) the last day on which a public company may send out copies` `the date of the relevant accounts meeting`) MINUS Day `the day the obligation arises`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "copies of the annual accounts and reports were not sent out at least 21 days before the date of the relevant accounts meeting"

-- src:5678 | (4) If in the case of a public company copies are sent out later than is required by subsection (3), they shall, despite that, be deemed to have been duly sent if it is so agreed by all the members entitled to attend and vote at the relevant accounts meeting.
@ref s 424(4) Late copies are deemed duly sent if all the members entitled to attend and vote so agree (src:5678)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `copies are sent out later than is required by subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is agreed by all the members entitled to attend and vote at the relevant accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 424(4) the copies are deemed to have been duly sent` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `copies are sent out later than is required by subsection (3)`
    THEN IF `it is agreed by all the members entitled to attend and vote at the relevant accounts meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "they shall, despite that, be deemed to have been duly sent if it is so agreed by all the members entitled to attend and vote at the relevant accounts meeting"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in the case of a public company copies are sent out later than is required by subsection (3)"; fork F21: the subsection is not engaged where copies were sent in time or by a private company

-- src:5680 | (6) In this section the “relevant accounts meeting” means the accounts meeting of the company at which the accounts and reports in question are to be laid.
@ref s 424(6) Meaning of "relevant accounts meeting" (src:5680)
GIVEN `it is the accounts meeting of the company at which the accounts and reports in question are to be laid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 424(6) the meeting is the relevant accounts meeting` MEANS
    IF `it is the accounts meeting of the company at which the accounts and reports in question are to be laid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the “relevant accounts meeting” means the accounts meeting of the company at which the accounts and reports in question are to be laid"

-- The whole of section 424, gathered by hand for a caller who asks "did the company send the copies out in time?"
-- (guidance of ruling E1, option B; every route is still answered by its own function above).
-- src:5672 | 424 Time allowed for sending out copies of accounts and reports
-- src:5673 | (1) The time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports is as follows.
-- src:5674 | (2) A private company must comply with section 423 not later than—
-- src:5675 | (a) the end of the period for filing accounts and reports, or
-- src:5676 | (b) if earlier, the date on which it actually delivers its accounts and reports to the registrar.
-- src:5677 | (3) A public company must comply with section 423 at least 21 days before the date of the relevant accounts meeting.
-- src:5678 | (4) If in the case of a public company copies are sent out later than is required by subsection (3), they shall, despite that, be deemed to have been duly sent if it is so agreed by all the members entitled to attend and vote at the relevant accounts meeting.
-- src:5679 | (5) Whether the time allowed is that for a private company or a public company is determined by reference to the company's status immediately before the end of the accounting reference period by reference to which the financial year for the accounts in question was determined.
-- src:5680 | (6) In this section the “relevant accounts meeting” means the accounts meeting of the company at which the accounts and reports in question are to be laid.
@ref s 424 Time allowed for sending out copies of accounts and reports (src:5672-5680)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which copies were sent out` IS A DATE
      `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company actually delivers its accounts and reports to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date of the relevant accounts meeting` IS A DATE
      `it is agreed by all the members entitled to attend and vote at the relevant accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 424(2) to (5) the company sent the copies out within the time allowed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 424(5) whether the time allowed is that for a private company or a public company` `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    WHEN `s 424(5) the time allowed for a private company` THEN
        `s 424(2) the private company sent the copies out in time` `the day on which copies were sent out` `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` `the date on which the company actually delivers its accounts and reports to the registrar`
    WHEN `s 424(5) the time allowed for a public company` THEN
        IF `s 424(3) the public company sent the copies out in time` `the day on which copies were sent out` `the date of the relevant accounts meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE `s 424(4) the copies are deemed to have been duly sent` TRUE TRUE `it is agreed by all the members entitled to attend and vote at the relevant accounts meeting`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 425: Default in sending out copies of accounts and reports: offences
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 425 Default in sending out copies of accounts and reports: offences`

-- src:5681 | 425 Default in sending out copies of accounts and reports: offences
-- src:5682 | (1) If default is made in complying with section 423 or 424, an offence is committed by—
-- src:5683 | (a) the company, and
-- src:5684 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 425(1) Offences by the company and by every officer in default (src:5681-5684)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 423 or 424` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 425(1)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 423 or 424`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "If default is made in complying with section 423 or 424, an offence is committed by— (a) the company"

@ref s 425(1) (src:5682)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 423 or 424` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 425(1)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`default is made in complying with section 423 or 424`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "If default is made in complying with section 423 or 424, an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is decided by section 1121

-- src:5685 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:5686 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:5687 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 425(2) Penalty for an offence under section 425 (src:5685-5687)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 425(2) the penalty for an offence under section 425` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection distinguishes conviction on indictment from summary conviction and does not distinguish the parts of the United Kingdom

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 426: Option to provide strategic report with supplementary material
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 426 Option to provide strategic report with supplementary material`

-- src:5689 | 426 Option to provide strategic report with supplementary material
-- src:5690 | (1) A company may—
-- src:5691 | (a) in such cases as may be specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State, and
-- src:5692 | (b) provided any conditions so specified are complied with,
-- src:5693 | provide a copy of the strategic report together with the supplementary material described in section 426A instead of copies of the accounts and reports required to be sent out in accordance with section 423.
@ref s 426(1) A company may provide the strategic report with supplementary material instead of the accounts and reports in cases specified by regulations (src:5689-5693)
GIVEN `the case is one specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any conditions so specified are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426(1) the company may provide a copy of the strategic report with the supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the case is one specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the cases are "specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State", which are not among the sources
    ELSE IF `any conditions so specified are complied with`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided any conditions so specified are complied with"

-- src:5694 | (2) Copies of those accounts and reports must, however, be sent to any person entitled to be sent them in accordance with that section and who wishes to receive them.
@ref s 426(2) Copies must still be sent to a person entitled who wishes to receive them (src:5694)
GIVEN `the company has provided the strategic report with the supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to be sent copies of the accounts and reports in accordance with section 423` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wishes to receive them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426(2) the company must send the person copies of the accounts and reports` MEANS
    IF `the company has provided the strategic report with the supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports`
       AND `the person is entitled to be sent copies of the accounts and reports in accordance with section 423`
       AND `the person wishes to receive them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any person entitled to be sent them in accordance with that section and who wishes to receive them"

-- src:5697 | (5) This section applies to copies of accounts and reports required to be sent out by virtue of section 146 to a person nominated to enjoy information rights as it applies to copies of accounts and reports required to be sent out in accordance with section 423 to a member of the company.
@ref s 426(5) Section 426 applies to copies sent to a person nominated to enjoy information rights (src:5697)
GIVEN `the copies are required to be sent out by virtue of section 146 to a person nominated to enjoy information rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426(5) section 426 applies to the copies as it applies to copies required to be sent out in accordance with section 423 to a member` MEANS
    IF `the copies are required to be sent out by virtue of section 146 to a person nominated to enjoy information rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to copies of accounts and reports required to be sent out by virtue of section 146"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 426A: Supplementary material
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 426A Supplementary material`

-- src:5699 | 426A Supplementary material
-- src:5700 | (1) The supplementary material referred to in section 426 must be prepared in accordance with this section.
-- src:5701 | (2) The supplementary material must—
-- src:5702 | (a) contain a statement that the strategic report is only part of the company’s annual accounts and reports;
-- src:5703 | (b) state how a person entitled to them can obtain a full copy of the company’s annual accounts and reports;
-- src:5704 | (c) state whether the auditor’s report on the annual accounts was unqualified or qualified and, if it was qualified, set out the report in full together with any further material needed to understand the qualification;
-- src:5705 | (d) state whether, in that report, the auditor’s statement under section 496 (whether strategic report and directors’ report consistent with the accounts) was unqualified or qualified and, if it was qualified, set out the qualified statement in full together with any further material needed to understand the qualification;
-- src:5706 | (e) in the case of a quoted company ..., contain a copy of that part of the directors’ remuneration report which sets out the single total figure table in respect of the company’s directors’ remuneration in accordance with the requirements of Schedule 8 to the Large and Medium-sized Companies (Accounts and Reports) Regulations 2008 ( S.I. 2008/410 ).
@ref s 426A The supplementary material referred to in section 426 must contain these statements (src:5699-5706)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the material contains a statement that the strategic report is only part of the company's annual accounts and reports` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material states how a person entitled to them can obtain a full copy of the company's annual accounts and reports` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material states whether the auditor's report on the annual accounts was unqualified or qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's report on the annual accounts was qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material sets out that report in full together with any further material needed to understand the qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material states whether the auditor's statement under section 496 was unqualified or qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's statement under section 496 was qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material sets out the qualified statement in full together with any further material needed to understand the qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material contains a copy of that part of the directors' remuneration report which sets out the single total figure table` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426A(2) the supplementary material contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the material contains a statement that the strategic report is only part of the company's annual accounts and reports`
            AND `the material states how a person entitled to them can obtain a full copy of the company's annual accounts and reports`
            AND `the material states whether the auditor's report on the annual accounts was unqualified or qualified`
            AND ((NOT (`the auditor's report on the annual accounts was qualified`)) OR `the material sets out that report in full together with any further material needed to understand the qualification`)
            AND `the material states whether the auditor's statement under section 496 was unqualified or qualified`
            AND ((NOT (`the auditor's statement under section 496 was qualified`)) OR `the material sets out the qualified statement in full together with any further material needed to understand the qualification`))
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F22): "The supplementary material must— (a) contain a statement ... (b) state how ... (c) state whether ... (d) state whether ..."
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- paragraph (e) is "in the case of a quoted company"; for any other company paragraphs (a) to (d) are the whole of the requirement
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the material contains a copy of that part of the directors' remuneration report which sets out the single total figure table`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F22): "(e) in the case of a quoted company ..., contain a copy of that part of the directors’ remuneration report which sets out the single total figure table"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is decided by section 385
